   "registered": "2026-09-28, before the workbench runner's first march",
   "measure": "the largest divergence, times dx / U, of the field each arm's own step produces every macro-step, before the freestream band is re-imposed, measured in the operator that enforced it: the full domain's own wide centred difference (the solver's last_div), and for a projected assembly the global projection's own spectral operator on the padded domain",
   "why": "both are projections, so what is left is round-off: the full-domain solver's Neumann mean-mismatch vanishes because the band holds equal velocities on opposite faces of the ring, and a spectral projection leaves ~1e-15. 1e-9 leaves six orders for accumulation. An assembly that is only a blend has nothing enforcing incompressibility after it, and fails this (L6/C2, W100). The band itself -- (U, 0) re-imposed in 8-cell strips after every step, W93's outer boundary -- is not divergence-free at its inner edge, identically in every arm, and is not what this measures",
